ard reached in 1:54.0.  After 400 metre splits of 53.0 and 59.8, it is evident that Sheppard was slowing considerably towards the end of the race, but even so, a differential of 1.2 seconds to cover the additional 4.68 metres between 800 metres and 880 yards seems unrealistic.  Having won the " [:a {:href "/results/56349"} "1,500 metres"] " seven days earlier, Sheppard completed a notable middle-distance double."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Melvin Sheppard would eventually win four gold medals in middle-distance running at the Olympics.  In 1908, he won the 800, 1,500, and ran on the " [:a {:href "/results/56432"} "medley relay team"] ", anchoring the 800 metre leg.  In 1912, he also ran on the " [:a {:href "/results/56690"} "4 x 400 metre relay"] ".  He eventually won five AAU titles over two laps – 1906-08, and 1911-12 –, and three Canadian titles – 1906, 1911-12."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79030"} "Mel Sheppard"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:58.0 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:52.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/72027"} "Emilio Lunghi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "1:57.2 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "1:54.2est (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70178"} "Hanns Braun"]] [:td {}